DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Page updated: Maine Judicial Branch Jury Stat
 us Notices
DESCRIPTION:This page's content changed since the last check. Visit the pa
 ge directly to review the update.\n\nWhat changed (text excerpt):\nAdded:\
 n  + All regular GRAND JURORS\, please report to the Capital Judicial Cent
 er on Thursday\, September 24\, 2026\, at 9:00 AM. No alternate Grand Juro
 rs are needed for September. Thank you and have a pleasant evening.\n  + S
 eptember 23\, 2026\n  + All jurors on Dupuis vs Robinson Hardware need to 
 appear on Thursday morning at 8:30 am. If you have any questions please ca
 ll 564-2240.\n  + September 23\, 0000\n  + Somerset County Superior Court 
 - Skowhegan\n  + All Jurors selected for Panel A in the matter of State vs
  Shaur\, need to appear on Thursday\, September 24th\, 2026\, at 8:30 am\n
   + You can park in the Skowhegan District Court\, Somerset Superior Court
 \, or the municipal parking lot. PLEASE DO NOT park directly across from t
 he Somerset Superior Court building. Thank you.\n  + PLEASE CHECK BACK HER
 E FOR ANY UPDATES TO THE ABOVE or CALL 1-800-872-5539 AFTER 6 PM THE NIGHT
  BEFORE YOU WERE TOLD TO REPORT.\n  + IF THE COURT NEEDS TO CLOSE DUE TO I
 NCLEMENT WEATHER A MESSAGE WILL BE PLACED AFTER 7:00 A.M\n  + PROHIBITION 
 OF ELECTRONIC DEVICES: Please be advised that pursuant to Administrative O
 rder JB-20-01\, use of electronic devices during trial or while in deliber
 ations are prohibited and all devices will need to be temporarily surrende
 red. During jury selection\, all devices must be turned off.\n  + Septembe
 r 24\, 2026\n  + All September Traverse Jurors are to check the jury statu
 s website or phone line on Friday\, September 25th after 5pm for further i
 nformation and reporting instructions.\n  \n[diff truncated]\nhttps://www.
 courts.maine.gov/juror/notice.shtml
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/juror/notice.shtml
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
